  "source_derivation_description": "This reference organ, Small-intestine-female (https://humanatlas.io/3d-reference-library) was created using data from\nthe Visible Human Dataset, provided by the National Library of Medicine (Spitzer and Whitlock 2002). The small\nintestines have been updated to include a measurement system. A centerline was made in the center of the intestines,\nand markers placed along the centerline. The teal discs measure 5 cm along the intestines, the green dashes measure 1\ncm. The yellow disc marks the jejunoileal junction. The Visible Human Female small intestine total length is 200 cm.\n\n**Bibliography:**\n\n* Spitzer, Victor M., and David G. Whitlock. 2002. \u201cThe Visible Human Dataset: The Anatomical Platform for Human Simulation.\u201d *The Anatomical Record* 253 (2): 49\u201357. https://doi.org/10.1002/(SICI)1097-0185(199804)253:2<49::AID-AR8>3.0.CO;2-9.",
